                             *   DU: $1 \\\\xrightarrow{D} 0                    
                             \\\\xrightarrow{U} 1$. OK.\\n                      
                             *   So 2 ways.\\n                    *             
                             $U=0, D=0$: 1 way.\\n                              
                             *   $U=2, D=3$: $\\\\binom{3}{3} =                 
                             1$.\\n                        *                    
                             Arrangement: DUDUD? No, 2 Ups, 3                   
                             Downs.\\n                        *                 
                             Possible: D U D U D.\\n                            
                             *   Check validity:\\n                             
                             *   Start 1.\\n                                    
                             *   D: $1 \\\\to 0$.\\n                            
                             *   U: $0 + 2^0 = 1$. (jump=1).\\n                 
                             *   D: $1 \\\\to 0$.\\n                            
                             *   U: $0 + 2^1 = 2$. (jump=2).\\n                 
                             *   D: $2 \\\\to 1$.\\n                            
                             *   End at 1. Valid.\\n                            
                             *   Any other arrangement? No, only 1              
                             way to place 3 Ds in 3 slots around 2              
                             Us.\\n                    *   Total so             
