                             4$.\\n                    *   Matches              
                             `count_ways_to_stair(1) == 4`.\\n\\n*              
                             **Hypothesis**:\\n    The number of                
                             ways to reach $k$ is the sum over all              
                             possible $U$ (number of Up moves) such             
                             that $2^U \\\\ge k$ and $D = 2^U -                 
                             k$:\\n    $$ \\\\text{Ways} =                      
                             \\\\sum_{U} \\\\binom{U+1}{D} $$\\n                
                             where $D = 2^U - k$.\\n    The                     
                             condition \\"no consecutive downs\\" is            
                             satisfied by the combinatorial formula             
                             $\\\\binom{U+1}{D}$, which counts ways             
                             to place $D$ items into $U+1$ slots                
                             (before, between, after Ups) with at               
                             most 1 per slot.\\n    Wait, the                   
                             formula $\\\\binom{n}{k}$ for                      
                             non-consecutive items is                           
                             $\\\\binom{N-K+1}{K}$ where $N$ is                 
