                             $\\\\binom{U+1}{D} = 0$. Since $2^U$               
                             grows exponentially, $D$ will                      
                             eventually exceed $U+1$ and stay                   
                             there?\\n    Actually, $2^U$ grows much            
                             faster than $U+1$.\\n    We need $D                
                             \\\\le U+1$.\\n    $2^U - k \\\\le U+1             
                             \\\\implies 2^U - U - 1 \\\\le k$.\\n              
                             Also we need $D \\\\ge 0 \\\\implies               
                             2^U \\\\ge k$.\\n    So we only need to            
                             check $U$ such that $2^U \\\\ge k$ AND             
                             $2^U - k \\\\le U+1$.\\n    Since $2^U$            
                             grows fast, the range of valid $U$ is              
                             small.\\n    For large $k$, $2^U                   
                             \\\\approx k$.\\n    Let\'s check the              
                             constraints. $k \\\\le 10^9$.\\n                   
                             $2^{30} \\\\approx 10^9$.\\n    So we              
                             only need to iterate $U$ up to around              
                             30 or 40.\\n    For each valid $U$, add            
                             $\\\\binom{U+1}{D}$.\\n\\n*   **Test               
                             Case Verification**:\\n    *                       
                             `count_ways_to_stair(512) == 1`.\\n                
                             *   $k=512$.\\n        *   $U=0                    
                             \\\\implies 1-512 < 0$.\\n        *                
                             $U=1 \\\\implies 2-512 < 0$.\\n                    
                             *   ...\\n        *   $U=9 \\\\implies             
                             512 - 512 = 0$. $D=0$.\\n        *                 
                             $\\\\binom{10}{0} = 1$.\\n        *                
                             $U=10 \\\\implies 1024 - 512 = 512$.               
                             $D=512$.\\n        *                               
                             $\\\\binom{11}{512} = 0$.\\n        *              
